ROLE: novelty_killer  VOTE: yellow

CLOSEST_PRIOR_WORK:
- {cite: "Wang et al. 2022, 'Text Embeddings by Weakly-Supervised Contrastive Pre-training' (E5)", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.03533", why_close: "Establishes the asymmetric 'query:'/'passage:' prefix that IS the underlying mechanism here. The claim's gain is this exact effect; it does not re-derive it. Mandatory cite — packet already cites."}
- {cite: "Su et al. 2022, 'One Embedder, Any Task' (Instructor) + Asai et al. TART", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2212.09741", why_close: "Instruction/prompt-conditioned embeddings — same family of 'the query needs its trained instruction.' Bounds the mechanism novelty to ~zero."}
- {cite: "Sentence-Transformers prompts + v3 release + v5 Router (encode_query/encode_document, config_sentence_transformers.json)", url: "https://sbert.net/docs/sentence_transformer/usage/efficiency.html (and prompts/ + v5 Router docs)", why_close: "The 'artifact self-describes + ST auto-applies' half is a DOCUMENTED ST feature, not a discovery. Novelty cannot rest on this half."}
- {cite: "MTEB PR#1221 'shipped prompt' support (Aug 2024)", url: "https://github.com/embeddings-benchmark/mteb/pull/1221", why_close: "Confirms even the benchmark scored without shipped prompts pre-2024 — supports the 'tooling lags the contract' narrative but also shows the seam is publicly known/tracked, not unseen."}

NAMING_VS_MECHANISM: The MECHANISM (prefix/instruction asymmetry helps retrieval) is fully known and honestly cited — zero mechanism delta. The genuine delta is narrow and lives on the INTEGRATION-DEFAULT axis: post-ST-v3 there is now a machine-readable contract (config_sentence_transformers.json) that ST honors via encode_query, so the failure survives a user who picked a self-describing model and used the standard DB path — that IS distinct from "you forgot the prefix" (pre-v3 there was no shipped contract to discard). BUT the framing is weaker than "DISCARD": pymilvus exposes query_instruction/doc_instruction, LangChain exposes query_encode_kwargs, LlamaIndex exposes query_instruction — the wrappers EXPOSE prompt params and merely default them empty / don't auto-read the artifact. So the true claim is "wrappers don't AUTO-LOAD the shipped prompt by default," not "wrappers make it impossible." That is a real tooling-default observation, but it is closer to a competent-bug-report than a mechanism discovery, and a hostile reviewer's "the param is right there, you just didn't set it" lands partially.

FATAL_COLLISIONS: None found. No paper or doc performs the specific audit (artifact self-describes → every prod DB wrapper drops it by default). No ≥2-source collision exists, so no KILL on collision grounds. (Caveat for L1: must confirm no CURRENT wrapper default auto-reads config_sentence_transformers.json — verified open for 4 as of 2026-06-04, but this is a moving target; a single vendor flipping the default closes the novelty.)

MANDATORY_RELATED_WORK: E5/Wang2022 (2212.03533); Instructor/TART (2212.09741, 2211.09260); Sentence-Transformers prompt + v3/v5 Router docs; MTEB PR#1221. Authors MUST frame the contribution explicitly as integration-default/packaging-seam, NOT as a new retrieval mechanism, and MUST acknowledge wrappers expose (empty-defaulted) prompt parameters so the claim is "no auto-load," not "no support."

RATIONALE: Not RED — mechanism is honestly cited (not re-derived), no fatal ≥2-source collision exists, and the post-v3 "shipped contract silently dropped by DB defaults, survives a competent user" framing is a genuine, if modest, delta on the tooling axis (the empty-prompt e5 control + alias-break control make it not a tautology). Not GREEN — the novelty is packaging/defaults rather than mechanism, and it is partially weakened by the fact that wrappers EXPOSE prompt params (so "DISCARD" overstates; "fail to auto-load" is accurate). The claim only earns advancement if it (1) re-labels itself as an integration-default seam with the four prior-art cites front-and-center, and (2) proves the default code path in situ (actual Chroma/pymilvus end-to-end producing the A-number) to lock the seam open across ≥2 models / ≥2 datasets. YELLOW.
